{
  "borough": "Wandsworth",
  "application_type": "Prior Approval",
  "decision": "Approved",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - This notice indicates that the proposed development would comply with conditions MA.2 of Schedule 2 Part 3 Class M of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 2015 (as amended) (\"the GPDO\"). \r\nIt is a requirement of condition MA.2(5) of the GPDO that the development must be completed within a period of 3 years starting with the prior approval date. \r\nIt is a requirement of condition M.A2(6) of the GPDO that any building permitted to be used as a dwellinghouse by virtue of Class MA is to remain in use as a dwellinghouse within the meaning of Class C3 of Schedule 1 to the Use Classes Order and for no other purpose, except to the extent that the other purpose is ancillary to the use as a dwellinghouse.\r\nIt is a requirement of paragraph W(12) of the GPDO that the development is carried out in accordance with the details provided in the application unless the developer and the local planning authority agree in writing.",
    "Condition : 2 - Prior to the first occupation of the development, details of the siting, design and materials of refuse and recycling storage to serve the development shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority. The refuse storage facilities shall be provided in accordance with the approved details prior to occupation of the development, and shall be retained thereafter. \r\nReason: In the interests of amenity and hygiene, in accordance with Council policy LP2 of the Local Plan (2023) coupled with the requirements of the National Planning Policy Framework. \r\n",
    "Condition : 3 - Prior to the first occupation of the development, the vehicle and cycle parking shown drawing number A_PL2_P_04 shall be provided and be retained for parking purposes for the users of the development and for no other purpose. \r\nReason: To ensure adequate provision is made for cycle parking in accordance with Council policy LP51 of the Local Plan (2023) coupled with the requirements of the National Planning Policy Framework.\r\n",
    "Condition : 4 - The ground floor sleeping accommodation finished floor levels must be set no lower than 5.69 metres above Ordnance Datum (mAOD), in line with the submitted Flood Risk Assessment by Southwest Environmental Limited dated July 2022; reference S20-529/FRA/A Revision 3\r\nThis mitigation measure shall be fully implemented prior to occupation and\r\nsubsequently in accordance with the scheme�s timing/phasing arrangement. The measure detailed above shall be retained and maintained thereafter throughout the lifetime of the development.\r\nReason: To reduce the risk of flooding to the proposed development, future occupants and not to increase flood risk elsewhere in accordance with Paragraph 170 of the National Planning Policy Framework and LP12 Water and Flooding of the Wandsworth Local Plan.\r\n",
    "Condition : 5 - INFORMATIVE: It should be noted that as the subject site forms part of Plantation Wharf development where there have been a significant number of prior approval applications for the change to residential units, the development as a whole fulfils the criteria for being excluded from applying for permits to any such future Controlled Parking Zone operating in this area. ",
    "Condition : 6 - INFORMATIVE: If cranes are required as part of the installation of the equipment, the applicant will need to liaise directly with the Heliport in accordance with current Civil Aviation Authority guidelines (https://www.caa.co.uk/commercial-industry/airspace/event-and-obstaclenotification/cranenotification/) and CAP1096 (https://caa.co.uk/cap1096)."
  ],
